reg_decoder_fld_t tof2_eth400g_pcs_rspec__sds_112g_fld_list[] = {
    { "mode", 3, 0, 0,0, 
      ". When set to 1, defines that Serdes is working in 112G mode. There is 1 bit per group of 2 logical lane:  - bit [0]: When set, configure logical lane 0/1 in 112G mode - bit [1]: When set, configure logical lane 2/3 in 112G mode - bit [2]: When set, configure logical lane 4/5 in 112G mode - bit [3]: When set, configure logical lane 6/7 in 112G mode" },
    { "rx_ckmux", 23, 16, 0,0, 
      "For each physical Serdes lane, defines which common clock is used when the Serdes is working in 112G mode. In 112G mode, each group of 2 lanes (0/1, 2/3, 4/5, 6/7) send 64 bits data on 2 groups of 32 bits + 1 clock bit. Those 2 clocks comes from the same source inside the serdes but have skew/uncertainty between them. Inside the Jbay die, this configuration select one of the 2 clocks as early as possible (to limit the complexity of meeting timing) :  - 0b: use the same clock as the lane clock (must be set to 0 for all non-112G mode) - 1b: use the clock from adjacent lane belonging to same group of 2 lanes Note that this register is physical, not logical and thus programming depends on rotation of IO Tile." },
    { "tx_ckmux", 31, 24, 0,0, 
      "For each physical Serdes lane, defines which common clock is used when the Serdes is working in 112G mode. In 112G mode, each group of 2 lanes (0/1, 2/3, 4/5, 6/7) send 64 bits data on 2 groups of 32 bits + 1 clock bit.This mux configures which one of the 2 clock of the Serdes is used as common source internally of JBay to send data/clock back to IO Tile.  Inside the Jbay die, this configuration select one of the 2 clocks as early as possible (to limit the complexity of meeting timing) :  - 0b: use the same clock as the lane clock (must be set to 0 for all non-112G mode) - 1b: use the clock from adjacent lane belonging to same group of 2 lanes Note that this register is physical, not logical and thus programming depends on rotation of IO Tile" },
};
